{"close() stops the commit thread before draining workers - any work items that complete during queue pool shutdown will have complete_offset called but no running commit thread to commit those offsets, causing message reprocessing on restart": 0.9424982070922852, "Double shutdown of shared queue_pool - ResultsStrategyFactory.shutdown() and SimpleQueueProcessingStrategy.close()/join() both call queue_pool.shutdown() on the same instance, creating unclear ownership and potential race conditions": 0.8823177814483643, "wait_until_empty checks queue depth (qsize) not processing completion - queue can reach qsize()==0 while a worker is still mid-execution on an item it just pulled off, causing misleading semantics": 0.8258834481239319, "get_committable_offsets iterates over full integer range from start to max_offset+1 - if there's a large gap between last_committed and max_offset (e.g., after partition rebalance), this loop could iterate over millions of integers while holding the partition lock": 0.7408139109611511, "join() on line 344 silently ignores the timeout parameter which callers may rely on": 0.7093904614448547}